  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>A family beach of about 350 metres between Cap Camarat and Cap Taillat (Ramatuelle tourist office), with fine sand and crystal-clear water. It is a public beach with free access, open all year, and the tourist office page lists parking, toilets and a restaurant nearby.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to the Ramatuelle tourist office (FAQ, 2025 "dog friendly" flyer and the beach page updated on 06/02/2026), all the commune's beaches, including L'Escalet, are open to dogs on a leash, all year round. No time slot is announced for dogs. Swimming is allowed except in the swimming-only zones (ZRUB); ask at the lifeguard posts, one of which is at L'Escalet in season.</p>
      <p>On the coastal path, access is tolerated for leashed dogs, as long as they stay on the path. The flyer asks owners to pick up droppings and lists bag dispensers in the commune.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: bring water and a bowl for your dog, and arrive early in summer, when the beach is busiest.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The <a href="/fiche-balade-cap-camarat-ramatuelle">coastal path links L'Escalet to Cap Camarat and its lighthouse</a>, a nice walk to extend the day on foot with your dog after a swim.</p>
